I found a (dated) article in Reuters about the recent shareholders
meeting.

If the poision pill provision is scrapped, doesn't that finally open
Digital for
a takeover ?

-----------------------------------------
Digital CEO Opposes Shareholder Proposals

BOSTON (Reuters) - Digital Equipment Chief Executive Robert Palmer said
he was opposed to proposals approved by shareholders to scrap a poison
pill provision and shorten the terms of directors. 

At the meeting, according to preliminary results, 65.5 million shares
were voted in favor of a proposal to declassify the board versus 22.4
million against, a company clerk said. 

Under the proposal, members of the board of directors and would be
elected annually, rather than face reelection every three years. 

Shareholders also voted in favor of a proposal to scrap or submit for
shareholder approval a stockholder rights plan, or poison pill, which
the company adopted in
1989. The vote was 61.3 million shares in favor versus 28.1 million
against. 

Shareholders voted in line with recommendations of the board against
shareholder proposals to hire an investment bank to explore any sale
opportunities and to have Palmer give up the presidency or the
chairmanship.



