> >After 3 years or so of NT/Alpha sales the NT/Alpha native software portfolio still standsat 25%
> >of the NT/Intel portfolio, this is not exactly exciting and will not re-assure MIS
> >types that NT/Alpha in not a risk when compared with NT/Intel.
>
> Hey, he might actually have something here. Yesterday I downloaded the
> trial version of the Microsoft Puzzle collection, and darn it if the
> system requirements didn't say "486DX2 (66MHz) or higher". Didn't stop
> me from running it on my Alpha, though. Likewise with the
> entertainment packs, or the original versions of Space Invaders/Donkey
> Kong/Pengo et al.
>
> Yep, there's a lot of software out there that will probably never have
