The following is a quick guide (In chronological order)

PC164  

Uses 21164A (EV56) CPU maximum speed 500MHz limited by chip set used (21172)
also known as Alcor2.
        
Uses Parity Fast Page Mode SIMMS (Not EDO & NOT SDRAM). 256 bit memory path as         
this compensates for a slow(ish) memory bus out of the Alcor2 chipset. 
128bit (ie 4 simms) can be used as well - set by jumper. 

ATX Format (Slightly non-standard (read early) caused by 
a) Lack of central screw near CPU
b) Lack of support of Soft - power reset - this is the biggest pain as
   it requires a PSU mod - you need to tie the Soft Power Reset line to low for
   for the system to work. As this is a mod on a mains powered device -                                 
   it's better to use a properly mod'ded supply. Recommend 300W min.
       
IDE on board with Serial & Parallel, PS2 Kbd & Mouse
        
1MByte of third level cache
        
1MByte of flash
        
Versions available with ARC console (For NT & Linux) or SRM licences (for D                 
Unix)
        
Supports NT4, Linux, Unix NOT OpenVMS (tho people may have gotten it to work,
there was no qualification work done.
        
    
PC164LX Sucessor to PC164

Uses 21164A (EV56) CPU maximum speed 600MHz supported to date. Uses 21174                         
Chipset aka Pyxis. Avvaliable in 466,533 & 600 bins, but the 533 is the only one
that is sensible.
            
Uses PARITY ie 72 Bit ie ECC SDRAM Non-Buffered, 3.3V. Up to 512MB.
        
128bit memory path
        
2MB tertiary cache
        
1MB flash
        
Supports new ALphaBios WinNT boot code - easier to use than ARC used in PC164
        
No Unix support as yet - coming. Supported by Linux.
        
Standard ATX PSU support. Can't remember about the holes.. 300W min rec.
        
IDE support as standard - uses same Intel Southbridge as PC164.
        
Faster motherboard than PC164 due to much faster memory subsystem and to a         
smaller extent, the larger cache.

Also sold by Samsung. 
        
        
PC164SX New baby on block

ONLY supports 21164PC (PCA56). As the package is quite a bit smaller on the PC         
than the standard variant, you will be unpleasntly suprised if you try to fit         
a 21164 to this board.. 
        
Same 21174/Pyxis support chip.
        
        
Certainly supports same meory as LX, but work is underway to qualify chealer 
non-parity SDRAMS as they PC chip actually does not use them However as there are no 
standards in the SDRAM world, it seems, check out DS's web site first.
        
1MByte SECOND level cache - and faster as well than the LX's 3rd level.
        
Cirrus Logic chip doing the south supplies EIDE, Ser, Par etc etc and         
eventually USB.
    
        
AlphaBIOS support & I am told MILO as well for the SX. Not known about DU.
        
Adds the Motion Video Instructions to the chip - enhancement for the arhcitecture that 
adds some features that make MPEG2 decoding possible in unaccelerated hardware - ie 
just a graphics card & a MPG2 stream. Other people will find alternative and 
interesting things to do with MVI once they find them..
        
Full ATX case support - holes, PSU & all - OK 250W min recommended as people will 
insist on configuring expensive & hot running HDD's and graphics cards in these 
puppies!
        
Codesigned with Mitsubishi.


Avaliable in speeds of 400Mhz & 533 Mhz. 466 got lost in a timing trap. 533 is top end
today.


Well maybe not so quick - got carried away.

Jim
        
        




