  Even I get tired of answering the "OpenVMS is dead" questions after
  a while.  There will come a date -- sometime in the future -- when
  there will be no general support available for Microsoft Windows NT,
  for UNIX, and for all of the other currently-available computer
  operating systems.  Ask me what that date is, and I can't answer.
  But I know there will be such a date.  Eventually.

  That said, OpenVMS engineering is still working on and is still
  developing new releases of OpenVMS, and -- for as long as there is
  sufficient profit in doing so -- OpenVMS will continue to be enhanced
  and will continue to be supported.  (RSX is still around and still
  supported, after all.)  And we -- OpenVMS engineering -- are hiring.
   
