Digital has one less thing left today.

CABLETRON SYSTEMS AND DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION ANNOUNCE STRATEGIC
PARTNERSHIP AGREEMENT 
 


ROCHESTER, N.H./MAYNARD, Mass., Nov. 25, 1997 - Cabletron Systems and
Digital Equipment Corporation today announced the signing of a
partnership agreement that includes the acquisition of Digital's network
product business unit and the establishment of reseller and services
contracts between Digital and Cabletron. The business will be operated
as a separate division within the Cabletron organization and will
provide both Cabletron and Digital customers with a full complement of
network products.  Digital will continue to provide services for Digital
products and will service Cabletron products in many geographies
worldwide.

Cabletron is acquiring the assets and technology of Digital's Network
Product Business for approximately $430 million in cash, stock and
product credits.  No other financial details were disclosed.  The unit
will be called the Digital Network Products Group:  A Cabletron Systems
Company.

Key elements of the agreement include: 

* Cabletron will provide current and future Digital-branded network
products, which Digital will sell to customers in addition to selected
products from the Cabletron product line;

* Digital has made volume commitments over the term of the agreement.

* Digital Worldwide Services continues to provide support for all
Digital-branded network products, and will also provide both warranty
and post-warranty service for Cabletron network products in many
geographies worldwide.


"With this first initiative, we are launching Cabletron's strategy to
rapidly expand through aggressive acquisitions and strategic
partnerships that extend our international presence and channel
distribution," said Don Reed, Cabletron's chief executive officer.  
"This agreement will bolster our core business, while linking us with a
strong partner for distributing Cabletron products to the enterprise and
service-provider markets.  Most important, Cabletron is acquiring a
business whose employees and products have established a first-class
reputation for quality and performance worldwide."

"This agreement represents an important example of Digital's focus on
solving customers' problems with the best available products and
services," said Digital Chairman Robert B. Palmer.  "We offer customers
the best solutions not only with our own products, but also through
partnerships and alliances with other leaders in our industry.

"Digital intends to be the world's preferred provider of Internet-based
enterprise solutions," Palmer added.  "Working with Cabletron, we will
continue to provide our customers with the world-class network products
they have come to expect from the Digital brand."

The acquisition is expected to increase Cabletron's international
revenues by between 35 and 40 percent, and its channel revenues by more
than 100 percent.   The network product business unit, with personnel
and offices throughout the world, currently does over 50 percent of its
business outside the United States and sells predominantly through
third-party distributor and reseller channels.  
The acquisition significantly increases Cabletron's presence in the
enterprise and telecommunications and Internet service provider markets.
With this agreement, Digital will expand its network solutions
capability by selling Digital-branded network products as well as
complementary Cabletron products. These products include switches,
routers, hubs, and network management capabilities.  

Digital retains the Internet and Web server product development
organizations, and the company's network research laboratories in Palo
Alto, California, and will be expanding network product support
services. 

The agreement is subject to receipt of government approval, including
the execution and delivery of definitive agreements and clearance under
the Hart-Scott-Rodino Antitrust Act.





