`Is that still legal'? is one I've heard applied to VMS.  (This was
surprise, during a workshop here, when someone from abroad noticed I was
using VMS and most other computers here were running UNIX.  The sad
thing is, my comment that my machine was the fastest in the building
didn't change his opinion of Digital.) 

> There's also the "don't believe a
> thing they say" factor.  

Right.  There have been so many requests from the newsgroups for some 
firm statement from Digital regarding things that we would like to hear 
and, although they have never been explicitly denied, the commitments 
are couched in a language which always leaves a back door open for a 
total about-face.  A while back, there was a REALLY NICE statement from 
a DIGITAL EMPLOYEE with NO DISCLAIMER ATTACHED saying that Digital would 
indefinitely support VMS.  Unfortunately, as many punters pointed out, 
`indefinitely' can mean forever (as I had hoped) but can also mean `for 
an indefinite period of time' which is probably the case since, after 
this was pointed out, no clarification was forthcoming.


