Recently, we'd had some performance problems with our
VAX 4000/100 running VMS 5.5-2 (ancient, I know..)
All of the sudden, the swap file would fill up within
5 hrs. of rebooting and produce login times of about 
literally 10 minutes.  The SHOW MEM/FILE command
showed *0* free pages left.  DEC stepped us thru
creating a second, larger swapfile which has 
made the system much more stable, and possibly
a tad faster.  

