Newsgroups: vmsnet.pdp-11,alt.sys.pdp11,comp.sys.dec,comp.sys.dec.micro


The 11/73 (Quad wide board) does have the ability to select the order of
attempted boots ...

In the Setup section, one of the boot setups (#6 if memory serves)
allows you to define the types of boot ...

"A" is teh standard MSCP boot of "try all MSCP devices in order of
removable then fixed"

You can replace that A with specific DU numbers ... like DU1 (for the
ZIP) followed by DU0

So that way if a boot of the ZIP fails it will default to the hard
drive.

Don't forget to save the settings to eprom before exiting setup, then
power down and power up the machine ... so you load the new settings.

Stuart



