         CABLETRON SYSTEMS AND DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
               ANNOUNCE STRATEGIC PARTNERSHIP AGREEMENT
 
 
     ...Cabletron acquires Digital's network product business...
     ...Digital expands networking solutions capability by selling
 Digital-branded network products and selected Cabletron products...
...Digital will also service Cabletron products in many geographies...
 
 
ROCHESTER, N.H./MAYNARD, Mass., Nov. 25, 1997 - Cabletron Systems and  
Digital Equipment Corporation today announced the signing of a 
partnership agreement that includes the acquisition of Digital's 
network product business unit and the  establishment of reseller and 
services contracts between Digital and Cabletron. The  business will 
be operated as a separate division within the Cabletron organization 
and  will provide both Cabletron and Digital customers with a full 
complement of network  products.  Digital will continue to provide
services for Digital products and will service  Cabletron products in 
many geographies worldwide.
 
Cabletron is acquiring the assets and technology of Digital's Network 
Product Business for approximately $430 million in cash, stock and 
product credits.  No other  financial details were disclosed.  The 
unit will be called the Digital Network Products Group:  A Cabletron 
Systems Company.
 
Key elements of the agreement include: 
 
o  Cabletron will provide current and future Digital-branded network 
   products, which Digital will sell to customers in addition to 
   selected products from the Cabletron product line;
 
o  Digital has made volume commitments over the term of the agreement.
 
o  Digital Worldwide Services continues to provide support for all 
   Digital-branded network products, and will also provide both 
   warranty and post-warranty service for Cabletron network products 
   in many geographies worldwide.
  
"With this first initiative, we are launching Cabletron's strategy to 
rapidly expand through aggressive acquisitions and strategic 
partnerships that extend our international  presence and channel 
distribution," said Don Reed, Cabletron's chief executive officer.   
"This agreement will bolster our core business, while linking us with 
a strong partner for  distributing Cabletron products to the 
enterprise and service-provider markets.  Most  important, Cabletron 
is acquiring a business whose employees and products have established 
a first-class reputation for quality and performance worldwide."

"This agreement represents an important example of Digital's focus on 
solving customers' problems with the best available products and 
services," said Digital  Chairman Robert B. Palmer.  "We offer 
customers the best solutions not only with our  own products, but also 
through partnerships and alliances with other leaders in our  
industry.
 
"Digital intends to be the world's preferred provider of 
Internet-based enterprise  solutions," Palmer added.  "Working with 
Cabletron, we will continue to provide our  customers with the 
world-class network products they have come to expect from the  
Digital brand."

The acquisition is expected to increase Cabletron's international 
revenues by  between 35 and 40 percent, and its channel revenues by 
more than 100 percent.   The  network product business unit, with 
personnel and offices throughout the world, currently does over 50
percent of its business outside the United States and sells 
predominantly through third-party distributor and reseller channels.  
The acquisition significantly  increases Cabletron's presence in the 
enterprise and telecommunications and Internet  service provider 
markets. 

With this agreement, Digital will expand its network solutions 
capability by  selling Digital-branded network products as well as 
complementary Cabletron products. These products include switches, 
routers, hubs, and network management capabilities.

Digital retains the Internet and Web server product development
organizations,  and the company's network research laboratories in 
Palo Alto, California, and will be  expanding network product support 
services.

The agreement is subject to receipt of government approval, including 
the execution and delivery of definitive agreements and clearance 
under the Hart-Scott- Rodino Antitrust Act.

Digital Equipment Corporation, recognized for product and service 
excellence, is  a leading supplier of high-performance, Web-based 
computing solutions that help  enterprises compete in the global
marketplace.  Digital offers its customers a winning  Internet 
advantage through a comprehensive portfolio of Internet solutions 
based on  award-winning systems, advanced networking infrastructure, 
innovative software, and  industry applications -- including those 
from its business partners.  The expertise and experience of Digital 
employees help customers plan, design, implement, manage and  support 
Internet solutions in countries throughout the world.  For the
latest company  information, visit Digital on the World Wide Web at

                           www.digital.com.

 
Cabletron Systems, a recognized leader in providing high-performance 
computer networking products, has provided dependable network access 
and communications to  millions of people throughout the world.  With 
scalable products designed for Fortune  1000 enterprise networks, 
service providers and small businesses, Cabletron provides  simple, 
reliable and cost-effective business solutions for the information 
age.

With corporate headquarters in Rochester, N.H. Cabletron employs over 
6,800  people worldwide.  Cabletron's common stock is traded over
the New York Stock  Exchange under the symbol CS.  Over the last four 
quarters, the company has reported  record revenue of $1.5 billion. 

Cabletron's World Wide Web site can be reached on the Internet at  

                            www.ctron.com.


