I'd certainly hope that the cash would go to the shareholders, so that
they'd get at least some return on their otherwise poorly performing
investment.  (And I'm talking about the regular shares, not the preferred,
although, if I remember correctly, the preferred holders go to the head of
the line when the final carving is done.) For the life of me I don't see
