I believe Akos's uVAX III is mounted in a BA23 (meaning it's probably an 
old II that's been upgraded at some point).  But I'm yet to see a Qbus 
device that can't be fitted into an S-box -- at worst you might need to do
a little metalwork to manufacture a distribution plate out of the S-box 
blanking plate or live with some cables hanging in odd places.  The reverse
conversion is usually possible as well, although it does tend to involve 
attacking functional parts with power tools to remove the integral 
distribution handles and a bit more metalwork to produce a BA23 panel insert.

Most conversions can be achieved with a drill and a good set of files.

