Digital's stock is always fluctuating up and down on that scale over that
time period - that's the whole problem, it just keeps going up and 
down without ever taking off.  That's because the company isn't growing and 
all you're seeing is trends in investor speculation (and lately a bit of 
price inflation due to the companies own stock buy back program). 
Companies that grow generally have stock values that grow with them.  Since
DEC shrinks, or stays the same size, holding DEC long term is a losing
proposition.  Never mind the one year return, how about the 5 and 10 year
returns on investment? 

