Yup.  You missed the fact that the DSSI node ID is separate and distinct
from the unit number.  The former can take on only values from 0 to 7,
and must be unique on a single DSSI bus.  The unit number, on the other
hand, is used to make the device name in VMS unique in a multiple-DSSI
bus configuration, where far more than 7 devices are possible.  VMS 
hides the fact that you have multiple-DSSI buses, and only presents
the device with the unit numbers visible.  So, these unit numbers must
be separately configurable.

Why your 3rd and 4th disks are reversed, I don't know, since by default
a new DSSI disk does indeed have the unit number set to the node ID.
I suspect that your "new" disk isn't really new, and one or more of
them have FORCEUNIT set, in order to override the default.



