The bus used for disks in a 4000-200 is DSSI.
If the machine is in its original case (ie. not moved to  a MV3400 case or so),
it should have three quite big  places for inserting disks over
the Q-BUS card cage (at least thats what a 4000-300 looks like).
There should be an edge connector in the back of each disk place.

According to Digitals Systems & Options Europe catalogue 1992 the alternatives
are:

RF31F-SF 200 MB
RF31E-SF 381 MB
RF35E-SF 852 MB
RF72E-SF 1 GB
RF73E-SF 2 GB

"SF" is for field installed variant.
There is also an "SA" variant which is factory installed.
No idea if there is any difference.

I guess an alternative would be to get an Q-BUS SCSI card.
No experience with that though.

