>Speaking of Intel, the pentium is a nice CPU... for me to poop on. What do
>people think about the showstopper bug making the rounds lately?

Not much.  Intel is giving it their usual arrogant brush-off, but
unlike the arithmetic errors they denied would ever actually happen,
this one only affects PCs that allow anyone to run a .EXE file.  It
can't take out a properly administered server because no competent
server manager would allow any riff-raff to log in.  All it can do is
halt a desktop PC.  It can't corrupt a boot sector, delete files, or
reproduce itself.  To recover, all you have to do is punch the reset
button and not run that .EXE file any more.  I wish recovering from
Microsoft's software crashes were that easy.

Of course, a virus could exploit this newly discovered bug, but there
are so many well known ways a virus can wreak havok that this is an
insignificant addition to the cyber-vandals' arsenal.

