The PPC 750's FPU problem is not going to affect anything unless an
application manages to execute a sequence of instructions that could
trigger the defect. It doesn't even affect all the PPC 750s. The trigger
for this is very artificial so unless you're actually aiming to trigger it,
it will very likely never happen. It will not crash the machine, and any
potential 'damage' to data would be limited to the particular process that
executes that code. No other processes would be affected at all. 

This is not in the same league as the Pentium bug. If you want to argue
that it is, you're a bloomin' loony. 

