This usually indicates one of two things:

	1) There is a problem with an application on your VAX that users
	   frequently use.  It is locking them up and they have no choice
	   but to attempt to improperly terminate their session.  Find out
	   if these users have an application in common... Many of these
	   problems can be resolved by simply raising limits on process
	   quotas in SYSUAF.
	2) Your network is broken.  I usually have to deal with hung port
	   issues after there has been some sort of break in the network.
	   (ie: cable down, or one of the routers bridging LAT goes down,
	   etc... oh.. and if you're bridging LAT over a POTS line, just
	   forget it.)

I work with DS300's often and have found them to be rather reliable...
Most of the time, the problem is with other connecting components in the
network, or with something happening on the system.

