Alex Hanks (ahanks@minicomputer.com) wrote:

: I am having a problem initializing some RZ28's and 29's after
: completing a low-level format. I continue to receive the same 
: confusing error message each time:

: "Unsuitable Cluster Factor" 

: Does anyone have some familiarity with this message?

Yes :-)

: If so, would you please shed a little enlightenment.

VMS allocates disk space in "clusters" which are groups of disk blocks (512
bytes). There is an architectural maximum number of clusters on any (FILES-11)
formatted disk. With large disks (for example the 9Gb drives I now use)
you need to set the cluster size to something larger than 3. In fact, the
required cluster size is given by 

	disk_size in blocks / (255 * 4096)

From memory (I'm not near my VMS cluster just now) I needed a cluster size
of 17 for the 9Gb drive. So assuming that the drive is called something
like dka100, the command would be

    $ initialize/cluster=17 dka100 my_disk

Hope this helps.
