Digital held its annual stockholder's meeting at the World Trade Center
in Boston today. The meeting was largely devoid of pyrotechnics. A
stockholder motion to separate the jobs of Chairman and CEO was defeated
by a three to one margin. A stockholder motion to retain an investment
bank to sell Digital was defeated by a four to one margin.

Palmer spoke at some length about the Digital/Intel settlement, but
refused to comment on a report in today's Wall Street Journal claiming
that Cabletron will purchase the Network Products Business Unit. (SKD
believes a sale or partnership will be announced Real Soon Now).

