If someone wants to tell a group something via any file, then she or he
should take care about the standard software used by the target group.
GhostScript (I also like to mention GV/Mainz) and XPDF are freeware and
not always installed on all systems. In my opinion it is not acceptable
to let people depend on unsupported freeware software. PostScript is more
common, especially because most printers are using PostScript today and
OpenVMS CDA viewer displays PostScript, too, like the mentioned freeware
tools. So I think it is more far-sighted to use an older (what ever this
