  In the upper left of many MicroVAX and VAXstation 3100 systems,
  you'll see a dimond-radius icon, indicating a SCSI connection,
  and (duh!) the SCSI connector.  

  In a rather poor graphics representation, the SCSI icon looks
  rather like this:

	 ^
	/ \
       <  --
        \ /
         v

  The rest of the widgets present on the back of the VAXstation 3100,
  across the bottom, from left to right, are:

	AUI Ethernet
	<Ethernet Interface Selection Switch>
	BNC Ethernet
	<Reset Switch>
	Keyboard (Modular jack)
	Mouse (DIN)
	Printer (MMJ; See OpenVMS FAQ for the MMJ pinout)
	Communications (MMJ; See FAQ for pinout)
	<S3> (alternate console selector)
	Status LEDs

