pmontgom@cwi.nl (Peter L. Montgomery) writes:
>	Using the cc and f90 compilers now present on Digital UNIX
>systems, how does one access UMULH (upper half of unsigned integer 
>multiply)?  [...]

In C:

  #include <c/asm.h>
  p = asm("umulh %a0, %a1, %v0", x, y);

or perhaps:

  #include <machine/builtins.h>
  p = __UMULH(x, y);

Then again you might prefer int_mul_upper().


>On the 21264, how will we access the population count
>and leading/trailing zero count instructions from Fortran and C?

  l1 = _popcnt(a);
  l2 = _leadz(a);
  l3 = _trailz(a);


>Inline code is desired for all of these.

And is produced, even for 21164, by recent versions of the C compiler.

-- Rob.

PS: Beware those who will jump down your throat for using stuff that
    isn't in their favorite "standard".



