Aside from the usual admonitions (like time the same sequence a few times,
keep the results in an array, and then do something with the array of times)
it seems to me that rpcc delays completion (not issue) for two cycles after
a st class instruction.  Other than that, it seems to yield cycle-accurate
data.  If you have problems with wrap-around, other timing methods will
give you accepable results because you are timing such long (>8 sec)
intervals.




