> <lots of shouting how mean Digital is deleted>
>But not so `small' that dec will not reengineer chips to be 
>NT-only so you CAN'T run VMS on them.

A myth. All Alpha chips so far have been capable of running all 4 operating
systems. There are only questions of firmware for boards.

>Pray tell, what is the EXACT difference between the -a, -au, and 
> -av workstations?

The -a has first pass 21174 chips, certain graphics and I/O controller.
The bugs in the pass 1 21174 are worked around for NT in the -a, but
it was deemed to difficult to do this for Unix and VMS, hence they're
using Pass 2 21174's.  Since different I/O options are supported by
NT and the other two OS'es, these also differ.

There isn't a -av workstation to my knowledge.

