>AXPpci 33 w/ 21066 @ 166Mhz
>1 MB 20ns L2 cache
>(2) 32 MB 60ns parity SIMMs
>S3 Virge PCI video card
>
>I connected up the mainboard power to a 250w P/S, connected the case
>speaker, a keyboard and a monitor.  Flip the switch, the power comes on
>and nothing.  Nada.  Bubkis.  I don't even get a video bios display on the
>monitor.  I mucked around with some jumper settings to correct what I 
>thought was an incorrect CPU setting, but still nothing.  I swapped out
>the S3 card for a basic Trident ISA VGA card.  No dice.
>
>I believe the board is getting power, because the heat sink on the Alpha
>starts to get warm.
>
>So, how can I troubleshoot this?  I'm used to Intel boxen, which give some
>indication through speaker beeps as to what the problem might be.  Right
>now I'm not sure where to start on this, and would appreciate any kind of
>assistance.
>

The first place I would try is looking at the jumpers - what you want
is to make sure it's not trying to send bootup stuff to com1.  The
design guide that should have come with the MB should have the
locations and settings of these jumpers (if you didn't get the design
guide, check out:
http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/axppci/read_me.html
)

Since you said you're used to using PCs, I think you'll also find:
http://www.azstarnet.com/~axplinux/
very interesting and helpful.  Note, however, that the boot sequence
is vastly different on an Alpha than on a PC.  If you need more help
feel free to email.

Jon



