"Britt Jensen" <dbjensen@usgypsum.com> writes:

> I was under the impression that crossover cables only worked for 10Mb
> networks.
> Anyway, I have tried it between two 3c905 equipped machines and it only runs
> 10.
> 
> I thinks 100Mb uses more than two pair of wire.

The common, garden variety of 100 Mbps UTP Ethernet (100Base-TX) uses
the same 2 pairs as 10Base-T. A cross-over cable works fine (although
it must be a Category 5 cable).

There is a spec in 802.3 for 100Base-T4, but there are few products
out there that implement it and it's not what people normally are
referring to when they speak of 100 Megabit Ethernet.

