   Alpha system.

   BTW, if you see "ESDRAM" in connection to future Alpha mother
   boards don't assume it means ECC SDRAM.  ESDRAM (Enhanced SDRAM)
   is a new memory technology that incorporates a small SRAM row cache
   on a DRAM chip.  This significantly reduces latency for page mode
   reads (10 ns vs 20 ns for example) and can make a big performance
   difference for some applications with poor cache behavior.

