> I am sure that had Digital dropped its plans for ALPHA and focused on
> VAX, it would probably have been able to get the same improvements on
> the VAX chip that Intel was able to squeeze out of the 8086. Digital
> invested instead on ALPHA so it is to be extected that VAX speed
> increases stopped because the reasearch went to ALPHA.

Intel has spent a ton of money to keep the x86 line competitive with
RISC chips; had Digital tried the same with the VAX--an architecture
that is *much* harder to pipeline--they would probably be bankrupt
now.  Intel can afford to throw tons of money at the x86 design
because of its huge market.  The VAX architecture never had a large
enough market to amortize the necessary costs, so it was far more
effective for Digital to switch to an architecture that could be sped
up at a price they could afford.
