What Andrew is probably thinking of is the STREAM bandwidth of the backplane
buses. While IBM certainly hasn't shown good numbers here in the past,
recent SGI and SUN machine indeed are quite good. Looking at STREAM
(http://www.cs.virginia.edu/stream/standard/Bandwidth.html) you
get:
------------------------------------------------------------------
Machine ID                ncpus    COPY    SCALE      ADD    TRIAD
------------------------------------------------------------------
DEC_8400_5-350               8   1026.7    986.1   1065.0   1132.3
DEC_8400_5-350               4    787.9    751.7    791.7    832.0
DEC_8400_5-350               2    420.3    399.8    424.7    451.2
DEC_8400_5-350               1    215.7    207.5    219.6    234.2
SGI_Origin_2000_2          128  21857.6  23351.7  24459.5  22913.6
SGI_Origin_2000_2           64  11470.6  11846.3  12696.2  12331.3
SGI_Origin_2000_2           32   5308.0   6534.0   6465.0   6539.0
