If you look over the last three years, you are finding that these records
got lost only relatively recently by Digital. You are correct that we had (and
still have) the CPU performance lead for three years straight. You are also 
correct that we have lost over the last 6-9 months one TPC result after the
other to the newest boxes and clusters of the named vendors (with the
exception of the newest SUN cluster result, never by a wide margin).

The newest SUN records though are more a question of software than
hardware. If I look at the TPC-C results for a UE6000 under Oracle 7
and Oracle 8 (23143 vs. 31147) you can see that your theory about hardware
superiority is a little far fetched.
newe

>The are lots of why's but one answer may be look at the backplane in the
