Oh well. Just in case:

	IA32 (x86) *is* a leading microprocessor architecture. It
	leads in numbers sold, applications available, vendors
	supporting it, foundries making compatible chips and overall
	revenue. 

IA-64 will be leading (even if vapour) at least in the following categories:

