The MIPS Decstations (I'm typing this on one...) were not performance
competitive with Alphas. I can run *all* user mode programs that this box 
(a DECstation 5000/240) *much* faster on any of our lab's Alphas (using
the MX translator). 

Alpha will retain performance leadership, hence VMS will.

>It gets much, much worse later on:
> . Digital will develop a full line of systems based on Intel's IA-64 
>   processor family. 
>Ie, the plan is to orphan Alpha systems, as with the MIPS DECstations.

I.e. you can't read English. It says that we , as a big vendor of Intel
systems (which we've been for years) do pre-jump the IA-64 server bandwagon
like all the other Intel system vendors. In case you didn't notice, the
Intel space of the spectrum lives off such long-distance statements.

