If there were any advantage for VMS on IA-64, we might even try it,
though it would be a lot more difficult to port it than NT or Digital
Unix. Why should we port VMS to a slower processor ?

>Moreover, 700 Million is a lot of money in absolute terms, but it's not 
>very much for the business that Digital is selling.  It seems order of
>magnitude to be about what Digital has invested, ie, where is the profit?

Read again. The fab was *exchanged* at book value, not sold
to make profit. That way it doesn't change the financial terms for both
companies too much.  We have tried to fill the fabs capacity for years
and didn't find partners to do so. Intel can do that easily.

> Here Digital is set to roll out Galaxies, so it 
