>Alpha's future, and all but announce that they will soon cease development
>on OpenVMS. 

Maybe we are just outright incapable of communicating to customers (well
I think that statement has some merit :-( ), but we introduced at lot
of *certainty* to Alphas future. No more issues around "can we afford
the fab ?" (there are three foundries now: Samsung, Mitsubishi, Intel).
No more issues around "can you replace Intel as the desktop leader to
get to volume ?" (we can for the high end of the desktop market, witness
the recent availability of Quark, CorelDraw, etc., we cannot for the mass 
market, as everybody except SUN is acknowledging).

